[Music]  commencement one of the most exciting  days of the year it's not too often you  have a family member or a loved one  graduating from MIT it's like inviting  somebody into your home you want it to  look good when the rhododendrons are  blooming it's beautiful  [Music]  it's really logistically challenging we  last year had 20 856 graduates and we  presented 2,300 pounds of diplomas  students get their diploma their piece  of history from the president of the  provost on stage to make that happen  is an incredible amount of work behind  the scenes our registrar staff is  preparing 2,500 plus diplomas to be in  exactly the right order we're very  careful and precise and it's a team  effort by a group of my staff there is a  great flux students are hoping to make  their diploma some do some don't so  we're continually monitoring advising  students they line up according to their  degree in school in alphabetical order  there's 70 station aides and then  there's a team of marshals that then  lead each of these specific groups out  to Killian court  [Music]  thank you they have to say their last  name and we'll be checking at that point  to make sure the student hasn't dropped  an invert 'only out of line or got lost  or something he is absent was but was  marked here yes my office keeps the  master list of the marching order there  is checks upon checks upon checks  because one student gets out of line  with a domino effect  jameelah s smith down as a graduate  crosses the stage they are handed their  actual diploma whereas many other  schools they're mailed their actual  diploma and their hand in a fake  certificate at the time of graduation we  want the students actually come off the  stage holding their actual degree so it  is a very flexible dynamic walking of  2,800 people to Killian Court  I've always felt that for MIT to do this  for their students says a lot about MIT  you quoi Elliot s Ishmael Rachel and  Hoffman  Athena why Kwang Lakeisha Jane students  will leave me the pronunciation of their  names on my voicemail  Amelie I know who you are  Maximiliano zuluaga Maximiliano  sebastian zuluaga the real trick is  getting where the emphasis is in  someone's name de mis w luck mojo and if  you place emphasis on the wrong syllable  then you can really botch a name Andrew  je-yoon and ER jinhwan lang it's not  just the complexity of an individual's  name but it's going from a Chinese name  to an Indian name to an American name to  a German name it's that switching from  one language to the other that can  sometimes be challenging Camille I henro  nagamma Nyak auntie Amy s Ishiguro  the ones who know they have a difficult  name when you get it right they smile  it's a good feeling  neaten center of Kumar Marie P olymbia  mu do one of the greatest challenges is  the  to set up 14,000 chairs takes hundreds  of people  basically what you're doing is taking  Killian Court and making it into a big  stadium  we set up these great big jumbo Tron's I  see a lot of really happy waving smiling  happy families out there for tens of  thousands of people around the world who  want to be a part of this special day  they can watch this on the webcast we  have about 250 volunteers each year that  handle different functions for our  guests making sure that they get into  the court having a good place that's it  having some information available we are  there to take care of the guests you  know make sure they know where they're  going they all have water they all have  programs they all have a seat we order  bottled water probably nearly 20,000  bottles  [Music]  this is New England the weather can go  to the extremes we have on hand 18,000  ponchos they are available to our  graduates too and we encourage them to  wear under their gowns the people that  come from other jobs because they  volunteer to do it it's really important  to them that all the chairs are straight  that everything looks beautiful and I  think that it gives them a sense of  serving the students and it makes them  feel good about their job  it gives time to pause and sort of think  wow what an amazing place to work and  how lucky I am to be part of such a  great experience congratulations  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

